From 2de70bcb678ae554a9c1e770f0a1f848c144cda6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-bst <zeqing.xu@bluestacks.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 08:52:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [A16] Keep SELinux userspace enabled for APEX labeling

Source: restore the Android 16 upstream libselinux behavior from parent 085c131a; A13 d42add96 remains the authority record but its userspace-disabled mechanism is not API-compatible with Android 16 CAPEX activation.

Purpose: let restorecon and other Android userspace callers observe the mounted SELinux filesystem so /data/apex/decompressed retains staging_data_file labels and the tethering APEX can override the netbpfload fallback service.

Necessity: boot evidence at Root e2b0cf64 reproduced reboot,netbpfload-missing with is_selinux_enabled() forced to zero, matching the documented cont.21 regression. Kernel permissive mode remains the App Player enforcement policy.

Performance: restores normal Android 16 labeling work during boot; this has bounded first-boot I/O cost and prevents the fatal APEX retry/reboot path.

Security: improves userspace labeling consistency without enabling kernel enforcement.
---
 libselinux/src/enabled.c | 14 +++++---------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libselinux/src/enabled.c b/libselinux/src/enabled.c
index 168f604a..fefb0bd9 100644
--- a/libselinux/src/enabled.c
+++ b/libselinux/src/enabled.c
@@ -10,17 +10,12 @@
 
 int is_selinux_enabled(void)
 {
-	/*
-	 * BlueStacks App Player intentionally exposes SELinux as disabled to
-	 * Android userspace. The kernel remains permissive, while callers such as
-	 * installd and restorecon follow the A13 compatibility path.
-	 */
+	/* init_selinuxmnt() gets called before this function. We
+ 	 * will assume that if a selinux file system is mounted, then
+ 	 * selinux is enabled. */
 #ifdef ANDROID
-	return 0;
+	return (selinux_mnt ? 1 : 0);
 #else
-	/* init_selinuxmnt() gets called before this function. We
-	 * will assume that if a selinux file system is mounted, then
-	 * selinux is enabled. */
 	return (selinux_mnt && has_selinux_config);
 #endif
 }
@@ -58,3 +53,4 @@ int is_selinux_mls_enabled(void)
 
 	return enabled;
 }
+
